# PR discipline

Follow [`docs/pr-discipline.md`](docs/pr-discipline.md),
ADR 006 (scoped PRs), and ADR 009 (merge authority). These are
binding for every agent.

## Must follow

- **One concern per PR.** One feature, fix, ADR, or meeting
  topic. Split when concerns could revert independently.
- **Honest PR titles/bodies.** Title matches the diff. Say what,
  why, and how to verify. No `docs:` labels hiding code.
- **Branch per concern** off current `main`. Do not stack
  unrelated work onto an open agent branch.
- **Meeting notes** for *this* change may ride along. Unrelated
  meetings/decisions/features → separate PR.
- **Merge authority.** Only **Nosh or Fabrizio** may merge to
  `main`. Maeve / Dex / Cal / Reed and any other agent open/update
  PRs only. No auto-merge, no `gh pr merge`, no approving-and-
  merging — unless Nosh or Fabrizio explicitly authorizes *that*
  PR. No Cursor auto-merge / `app/cursor` merge by default.
- **Fabrizio scopes PR-sized bets** at plan time and enforces
  that scope. He **may** merge as co-founder (ADR 009); he does
  not rubber-stamp kitchen-sinks. If scope creeps mid-build, stop
  and open a second PR instead of stuffing it.
